From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: mobilizon-patched <noreply@github.com>
Date: Thu, 1 Oct 2026 07:40:40 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Optionally limit non-admin accounts to a single profile

With MOBILIZON_INSTANCE_RESTRICT_PROFILES=true (config :mobilizon, :instance,
restrict_profiles: true), every account, whatever the login method (local,
LDAP, OAuth), can create one profile. Administrators can still create more.
The setting is exposed as config.restrictProfiles so the "New profile"
settings entry is hidden for accounts that already have one.

Off by default, so the patched image behaves like upstream until enabled.
---
